      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Great work tracking this down. We hit this exact same `QK_I2_S` block layout mismatch (64 vs 128 elements) when building the ARM NEON `vdotq_s32` kernels for [Project Zero](https://github.com/shifulegend/project-zero). \n\nWhen the layout is hardcoded to 64 on AArch64, it halves the outer block stride, feeding misaligned offsets into the row traversal. We eventually solved this class of bugs by enforcing a strict interleaved C99 layout and using runtime SIMD dispatch (AVX2 / NEON / scalar) rather than `#ifdef __ARM_NEON` compile-time layout switches, keeping the core architecture-invariant.\n\nGlad to see the pinned submodule is picking up the fix — isolating that degeneracy across architectures is not easy!",
