      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Thanks, good to know we weren't the only ones who hit this. You're right that runtime dispatch with one interleaved layout is the cleaner fix. I kept this one as a compile-time #elif so it stays small and easy to review against the pinned submodule, but a single arch-invariant layout that only swaps the kernel is the better structure, and that per-arch drift is what caused the bug in the first place. I'll take a look at how Project Zero handles it if this grows past a point fix.",
